WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.580
Star Trek vs. Star Wars.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.040
Batman vs. Superman.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.740
SCP-096 vs. SCP-682.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.310
We just can't seem to resist pitting icons
against each other.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:13.519
What can we say?

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:18.650
It's fun to see how two powerful forces would
go up against each other, and which one would

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.850
come out on top!

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:25.050
Fortunately, at the SCP Foundation, we can
justify pretty much anything by saying it's

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.289
for research purposes.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:30.630
Trying to make infinite money using SCP-914?

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.020
That's just research!

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.520
Giving a can of soda to SCP-999 to watch it
bounce off of the walls?

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.520
Research.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.950
Making infinite margaritas with SCP-294 while
you're still on the clock?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.230
It's totally fine, Ethics Committee!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.000
It's just research!

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.590
Putting two SCP Foundation Mobile Task Forces
together and making them fight isn't playing

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.809
God and risking lives for your own petty amusement.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:57.000
It's, say it with me now: research!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.550
More specifically, it's cross-testing.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:05.119
Sure, that term generally only applies to
SCPs, but people who ask too many questions

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:08.110
don't survive long at the Foundation.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.750
Instead, let's talk about the answers to a
question we posed to all of you.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.850
What if cross-tests were done on Mobile Task
Forces?

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.100
Which specialized groups would you test with
one another?

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.960
What kind of chaos do you think would ensue?

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.810
We asked our community here at SCP Explained
for your ideas, and you all really let your

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.360
creativity shine!

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.140
So, without further ado, let's see what happens
when we pit spy against spy, brain against

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:40.440
brawn, or the cold, calculated expertise of
the Red Right Hand against the unpredictable

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.810
nonsense of Dr. Bright.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:47.960
Sharky Reynolds said, "I can't imagine MTF
Lambda-5 (White Rabbits) losing to any other

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.280
Mobile Task Forces.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:57.280
I mean, being the first ones called if SCP-953,
SCP-106, or SCP-239 break containment and,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.850
worst of all, working with Dr. Clef has got
to make their tolerance for pain through the

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.850
roof.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:08.170
However, if I were to cross-test them with
one, I'd have to go with MTF Epsilon-9 (Fire

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.240
Eaters).

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.020
Something about a team trained to handle reality
warpers VS.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:16.710
a team whose dreams of becoming Firebenders
kind of coming true sounds epic to me.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:20.940
(On a side note, in a previous video that
also I provided a comment for, "Which SCP

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.720
Mobile Task Force Would You Join?", that radio
neutralizing MTF Lambda-5 agent looked shockingly

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.250
similar to me.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.750
Should I be worried about the possibility
that the foundation knows what I look like,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.819
or that I may have just made Dr. Clef angry?)"

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:39.260
Resemblance to any existing commenters is
purely coincidental and not intentional on

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.050
the part of the SCP Foundation or any affiliated
YouTube channels.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.390
Did I get that right, Dr. Clef?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.230
Do you promise to leave my family alone?

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.530
Please, put down the chainsaw.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.900
Back to your original point, seeing the White
Rabbits face off against the Fire Eaters would

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.390
certainly make for an explosive event!

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.390
Get it?

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.240
Because of the...fire...?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.240
Moving on.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.989
Chase Frost said, "Pandora's box vs Samsara,
they would be comparable.

00:03:05.989 --> 00:03:10.080
Alpha-1 and Tau-5 would go to samsara every
time.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.870
Samsara vs Able, and his hand-picked team
mates (whom could easily surpass Alpha -1

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.670
in skill) would be far more comparable.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.850
Anomalous humanoid (and some of the most highly
skilled human combatants) vs anomalous cyborgs.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.730
How could you turn that test down?"

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:28.379
Pandora's Box was technically disbanded following
the disastrous outcome of trying to harness

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:34.019
Able's bloodlust for the purposes of the Foundation,
but you can never rule out a reunion!

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:38.050
And an unkillable warrior with an insatiable
thirst for violence up against four cyborgs

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:42.099
made from clones of the flesh of a dead god,
with minds that can survive and be recovered

00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:44.000
even if their bodies are destroyed?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.140
That's the crossover of the century.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:50.290
And, since no one involved can truly die,
it's a battle that would probably go on for

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.370
a century or more, too.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:58.650
Jason Gutmann said, "Set Epsilon-11, "Nine-Tailed
Fox" against Nu-7, "Hammer Down" and see what

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.510
sort of armageddon would result from it, probably
involving heavy artillery, tactical combat

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.400
skills, and a couple nukes."

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:10.230
No thaumatology or reality warping here, just
good old-fashioned combat and a couple of

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.230
nukes.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.930
I'd say that I like the way you think, but
it honestly just makes me kind of nervous!

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.660
No launch codes for you!

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:23.600
Unknown- how mysterious - said, "I am gonna
say the most obvious one, Alpha-1 (The Red

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.460
Right Hand) vs Omega-1 (The Law's Left Hand).

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.850
Two perfectly opposite groups.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.180
One headed by the O5 Council and the other
by the Ethics Committee.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.050
I seriously want to know how this will work
out.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.020
Plus, there is a high chance that it has happened."

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:44.600
As equal opposites serving special interests
that frequently butt heads, it's entirely

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.120
possible these two groups have already gone
to war with each other in the past!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.110
It's hard to say, since the Red Right Hand
would probably never let the story get out.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:56.360
In fact, someone is looking at me through
the window right now and making a very threatening

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.740
gesture that makes me think I should stop
talking about MTF Alpha-1 immediately.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:02.740
Moving on!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.990
Katsen said, "Oh!

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:10.169
MTF Mu-13 “Ghostbusters” vs MTF Omega-0
“Ará Orún”.

00:05:10.169 --> 00:05:14.720
Omega-0 are the “saints” of the Foundation,
the memories of dead foundation employees,

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.780
and depending on your interpretation, pretty
much ghosts working for the Foundation.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.660
This would be a cross test!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.440
Samsara vs Hammer Down would be one for the
ages as well.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:29.289
I’m also curious how the City Slickers and
Village Idiots would fare against each other!"

00:05:29.289 --> 00:05:33.919
You're far from the only commenter who proposed
pitting Samsara and Hammer Down against each

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:34.919
other.

00:05:34.919 --> 00:05:38.490
In general, it seems that folks really want
to see Samsara fight with other Mobile Task

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:44.100
Forces, and it's easy to see why, since the
result would pretty much be an SCP-themed

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.410
Terminator movie on steroids!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.680
But I'm more interested in the other pairings
you suggested.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:54.389
Ghostbusters vs. what are essentially the
ghosts of the Foundation itself is too interesting

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:55.389
to ignore!

00:05:55.389 --> 00:05:59.550
Meanwhile, Village Idiots vs. City Slickers
would be the perfect chance to see once and

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.690
for all if it takes more skill to contain
anomalies in the city or in the country.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:09.860
Brandon Muzer said, "Lambda-5 ( white rabbits)
is my favorite mtf squad because I feel like

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:14.330
they would have to deal with the craziest
missions the SCP foundation has to offer and

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.169
we don’t get to see enough of them.

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:20.590
In would like to see them be cross tested
with omega-12 ( achilles heels) because they

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.660
are composed of reality benders, should be
fun and convoluted."

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:29.810
The White Rabbits specialize in navigating
unstable, surreal, and controlled reality,

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.990
and containing potentially dangerous persons
and artifacts capable of manipulating space

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.520
and time, while the Achilles Heels are a team
made up of reality-bending personnel from

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.540
an alternate universe.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.449
Fun and convoluted is an understatement, as
a cross-test of the two might just result

00:06:46.449 --> 00:06:48.600
in reality itself collapsing.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:52.820
But hey, at least it would be entertaining
before everyone turned inside out or we all

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:57.020
fell into an alternate dimension filled with
giant shrimp or whatever.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.669
Somebody - No, seriously, that’s their name
- said, "I would like to see Epsilon-9 "Fire

00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:07.080
eaters" and Delta-14 "Winter Wonderland" They
have the opposites of jobs one is for fire

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.510
and another is for winter i like to see them
fighting"

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:12.130
Fire vs. Ice.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.419
Simple, elegant, I like it.

00:07:14.419 --> 00:07:16.349
Wouldn't know what to wear for that battle
though.

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:21.580
I'm thinking safety goggles, snow pants, and
flip-flops?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:25.650
Commander Toolbelt said, "I would like to
see alpha 1 (the red right hand )meet the

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:31.150
bright 99 (oh no you don'ts) I just think
it would be funny seeing a super serious mtf

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:35.960
meet the goofy goobers that have to deal with
over 300 dr brights lol"

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.289
After all this time, the age-old question
would be put to rest: What's more dangerous,

00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:45.000
physical violence, or the psychological toll
it takes to interact with 300 Dr. Bright's

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.000
all at once?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.919
I say it depends on who gets a head start,
and if the Dr. Brights have access to any

00:07:49.919 --> 00:07:50.919
props.

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:54.889
You should see what Dr. Bright can do with
a rubber chicken and a hand grenade.

00:07:54.889 --> 00:07:56.169
It's not pretty.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:01.990
Derek McDaniel said, "MTF-Zeta 9 (Mole Rats)
vs MTF-Lambda-12 (Pest Control).

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:06.711
I’m curious how would Lambda-12 that has
never lost a single operator (as far as I

00:08:06.711 --> 00:08:12.020
know) fair against the Molerat team who face
so many unimaginable horrors that they probably

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:16.830
have the highest death counts out of all the
task force, and maybe the most experienced

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.270
veterans in the SCP Foundation."

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:23.770
The monotony of pest control vs. the unfathomable
horrors of the deep underground.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:29.080
Honestly, instead of having them fight, maybe
we could just give both groups a free counseling

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.740
session instead.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:32.810
Hannah Quintua said, "Hmm.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:39.890
Eta-10 "See No Evil" which is for visual anomalies,
and Eta-11 "Savage Beasts" is for auditory

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:40.890
anomalies.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.269
Let's see them work together."

00:08:42.269 --> 00:08:45.550
A collaborative cross-test, rather than a
battle!

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.250
I like the way you think!

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.310
Putting those two groups together to handle
a mission as one would either be extremely

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:55.850
successful, or result in the auditory anomalies
harming Eta-10 while the visual anomalies

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:59.780
went after Eta-11, knocking both groups out
at once.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.310
Only one way to find out!

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:08.070
Wooper Gamer said, "MTF Lambda-14 ("One Star
Reviewers") VS MTF Rho-9 ("Technical Support").

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:12.120
Neither of them likely have any fighting experience,
so it’s a fair fight."

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.019
Now that's what I'm talking about!

00:09:15.019 --> 00:09:18.700
Some viewers want to see the most effective
combatants working for the Foundation go toe

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.930
to toe, but not you.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:25.490
You want to throw two groups with basically
no combat experience into the ring together,

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.350
and see what happens next.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:32.260
It would be one of the most low-stakes fights
in Foundation history, negative Yelp reviews

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:36.880
and "can I speak to the manager" vs. hacked
Instagram accounts and those annoying emails

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.980
that say "forward this to ten friends or you'll
be cursed!"

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:44.190
Or you could just give everyone a weapon,
take their computers and phones, and see what

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.610
happens next.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:50.690
Linc said, "We gotta see Alpha-1 “Red Right
Hand” vs Nu-7 “Hammer Down.”

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.510
Alpha-1 is a highly sophisticated MTF Unit,
dedicating and risking their lives to save

00:09:55.510 --> 00:10:01.110
the 05 Council, doing insanely risking tasks
that involve years worth of training not only

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.370
in fighting, but stealth too.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.399
Meanwhile Nu-7 doesn’t give a damn about
stealth and just goes balls to the walls."

00:10:07.399 --> 00:10:11.870
The resulting conflict would probably decimate
cities and fell national governments, but

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.080
it sure would be entertaining to watch!

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:20.850
FalconFig said, "I'd honestly like to cross
test my favorite MTF-Beta-777 (Hecates Spear)

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:26.070
and MTF-Gamma-6 (Deep Feeders) and see them
fight off deep sea eldritch entities.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:31.620
Considering how Beta-777 specializes in thaumaturgical
combat, countermeasures, and rituals; they

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:36.540
would be very useful with Gamma-6 if something
like that scenario were to happen."

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.200
Another collaborative cross-test!

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:43.260
Hecate's Spear specializes in thaumaturgical
ritual analysis and countermeasures, while

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:48.600
the Deep Feeders specialize in the investigation
and tracking of deep-sea or oceanic anomalies.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.560
In order for something to require both of
their skill sets, things would have to get

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.519
pretty darn Lovecraftian!

00:10:54.519 --> 00:11:00.620
And I mean the real deal, not a super chill
Gamer Cthulu like SCP-2662.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:04.480
Some real, mind-breaking cosmic horror rising
up from the deep.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:10.080
Broad ford said, "I would find it really interesting
to put Delta-5 (front runners) against Sigma-66

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.620
(sixteen tons).

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:17.870
An MTF that specializes in infiltrating GOIs
going against an MTF that is made up of GOIs

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:20.709
sounds really appealing to watch."

00:11:20.709 --> 00:11:25.240
Captured members from existing Groups of Interest
going up against a group dedicated to infiltrating

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:29.440
those same Groups of Interest would definitely
be appealing to watch!

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:34.110
But it would probably get a bit awkward too,
as more than a few covers wind up getting

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.399
blown.

00:11:35.399 --> 00:11:39.860
Imagine working side by side with a guy in
your secret organization for years, only to

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:44.649
get captured by the SCP Foundation and find
out that same guy was working for them all

00:11:44.649 --> 00:11:45.649
along!

00:11:45.649 --> 00:11:48.080
Bob was a traitor all along.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.139
Even when he signed your birthday card.

00:11:50.139 --> 00:11:52.550
Even when you did a duet together at karaoke.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.480
You wonder, was any of it real?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.860
He promises that he really did see you as
a friend, not just a coworker and a means

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:03.370
to gather secret intel for the Foundation,
but some wounds never heal.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:08.300
Dino Tales said, "I would have to say MTF-Θ-10
"Troops of Literature" (文字部队) and

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.519
MTF Tau-5 ("Samsara").

00:12:10.519 --> 00:12:14.600
Who's better to take on narrative anomalies
and author entities than a team of cyborg

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.399
demigods they created."

00:12:16.399 --> 00:12:21.950
Kind of a chicken or the egg situation there,
only instead of chickens and eggs it's incredibly

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:25.399
powerful supernatural cyborgs and creative
anomalies.

00:12:25.399 --> 00:12:29.800
This fight would give a whole new meaning
to Death of the Author, that's for sure.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:36.490
Derek McDaniel said, "MTF-Iota 10 (Damn Feds)
vs MTF-Pi-1 (City Slickers).

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:41.500
The two task forces (at least that I know
of) that work in urban environments and in

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.500
undercover.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.050
How would these two face each other one way
or another?"

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:46.630
I can see it now!

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:51.000
The feds driving in nondescript black cars,
tailing the City Slickers down crowded streets.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:55.190
I'm not sure why they'd be doing that, but
I really want to see a car chase, and this

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.950
seems like the best pairing to make it happen.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:02.180
SolarKingYT said, "10 to 1 that any of them
would just sit down and have a coffee"

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:06.829
When you think about it, all of these groups
have way more in common than not.

00:13:06.829 --> 00:13:11.209
They all work for the same faceless organization,
they all deal with life-threatening anomalies

00:13:11.209 --> 00:13:12.600
in their own way.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:16.350
Maybe instead of thinking about how they'd
fight, we should just let them kick back for

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.520
once, relax, and swap stories over a hot cup
of Joe.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.709
Just...don't use SCP-294 to make it.

00:13:23.709 --> 00:13:25.100
That could get bad fast.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.930
Let them go to a Starbucks or something.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:32.630
Now check out “SCP Elite Mobile Task Force
Explained” and “Which SCP Mobile Task

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:33.800
Force Would You Join?” for more!

